 "about": {
  "text": "Paerau and Patearoa are two small power stations on the upper Taieri River in Otago, both opened in 1984. In winter they run on the river's natural flow. In summer Paerau uses water stored for irrigation in the Loganburn Reservoir and released down the Taieri, while Patearoa runs only when there is water to spare.",
